@pcbeingused333 Thanks for asking first. We'd go with (2) too. It fixes every member #1501 is about, with no list to keep up as the agent and rule text changes, and a pull then does what `recall disable` already does. The cost is that a copy a member edited is also removed. Since the team turned recall off, we think that's acceptable, and the old warning about an edited copy goes away with it.

@jeff-r2026 This one is your call: remove the recall agent and rule by name when a pull finds recall off (the same as `recall disable`), or keep the "only if unedited" check plus a list of past releases' copies.
